---
Aelius: It's been... a rough time.
Aelius: There isn't a day that goes by that I don't miss her.
Aelius: ... My mom.
Aelius: Cooking has helped keep my mind off things, as much as it hurts to not have anyone to share it with anymore.
Aelius: My dad… he was never in the picture. Never met him and mom never spoke of him….
Aelius: *<i>Sigh</i>*
Aelius: No use worrying over nothing.
Aelius: Tomorrow is another day.
Aelius: … Maybe I’ll cook her old tuna recipe.

// CLOUD BG, AELIUS
<<Act "Aelius" "Aelius 3_4s" "left" "bottom" #674ea7>>
Mother: Aelius, dear?
Aelius: [Negative] ... Mom?
Aelius: [Negative] Where are you?
Aelius: [Negative] (<i>I don't see her anywhere.</i>)
Mother: The weather is so nice today, don’t you think?
Mother: We should enjoy it. Could you make some of that <b>Hippocampus Lemonade</b>?
Aelius: [Negative] (<i>Sounds just like her... gods, I wish she was really here right now.</i>)
Aelius: ...
Aelius: You did always love that.
Mother: There’s nothing better to drink under the warmth of the sun, I’d say.
Aelius: … I’ll get right on it, mom. Just hang on for a bit.

// Cooking bg
<<Hide Aelius>>
Aelius: (<i>Haven't made this in a while. Not since she passed...</i>)
Aelius: (<i>Let's see if I still got it.</i>)
// LEMON SQUEEZING HERE
Mother: Mm, I already can't wait.
Aelius: (<i>It's so nice to hear her voice again. Like she's still around. </i>)
Aelius: (<i>...And not as weathered from her illness as it was near the end.</i>)
// LEMON SQUEEZING again
Aelius: (<i>It sounds like she's just behind me, like she alwayss was when I cooked.</i>)
Aelius: (<i>... I wish I could believe it was her.</i>)
Aelius: (<i>But she’s passed on, taken by her illness; and I know that.</i>)
Aelius: (<i>I just wanna see her again, see her as she was. But if I turn around…</i>)
Aelius: (<i>I know she won’t be there. I can’t deal with that hurt all over again.</i>)
Aelius: (<i>I just… I wish I could cook for my family again.</i>)
//MIXING
Aelius: (<i>It’s done. At least it still looks good.</i>)
Mother: Wait, Aelius. Before you serve it.
Aelius: Yeah, mom?
Mother: Feel the recipe, dear. Feel it within you.
Aelius: ... Okay.
Mother: Channel that feeling. Put your everything into the dish.
Aelius: How?
Mother: Just try it, dear.
//CAST STEP
Aelius: I- I... I don't get it. What was that?
Mother: A final touch - to give the dish what it needs.
Mother: Now, could I please have a glass?
Aelius: Yeah, um... yeah.

//AELIUS FREEZES

//CLOUD BG, AELIUS AND Hestia
<<Act "Aelius" "Aelius 3_4s" "left" "bottom" #674ea7>>
<<Act "Hestia" "Hestia 3_4s" "right" "bottom" #e06666>>
Aelius: Are you... a <i>god</i>?
Hestia: I supposse I am. I'm glad to finally make your acquaintance, Aelius.
Hestia: I've heard a lot about you.
Aelius: This isn’t… this is a dream. You’re not really here. This is not happening.
Hestia: I understand your confusion, my dear. But I can assure you, this is real.
Hestia: You wish to cook for your family again?
Aelius: How did you…? Nevermind.
Aelius: ... Yeah, I do.
Hestia: I can aid you in that, Aelius.
Hestia: Come work for me at my diner. We could use someone with talents like yours.
Aelius: <i>You</i> own a diner? I didn't think godss need to even eat.
Hestia: *<i>Laughs ssoftly</i>* Yes, but it's not what you're thinking, I'd wager.
Hestia: It’s a diner for the Olympians. Located on Mount Olympus, of course.
Aelius: <i>Mount Olympus</i>? And you're inviting <i>me</i>?
Hestia: Yes, my dear.
Hestia:  I can give you time to consider, if you’d like.
Aelius: ...
Aelius: (<i>This is really happening. I’m standing in front of one of the gods. And she wants my assistance. Me, of all people.</i>)
Aelius: (<i>It’s hard to wrap my mind around it. But I can tell she’s serious. It would be a big change…</i>)
Aelius: (<i>But a chance to cook for my mom again… I find it hard to resist.</i>)
Aelius: [Negative] (<i>It’s not like I have much for me here anymore, anyways.</i>)
Aelius: ... I'll go.
Hestia: Excellent, my dear. It will be a joy to have you.
Hestia: I’ll give you the day to gather yourself. Come dusk, I will return for you.
Hestia: I look forward to seeing you again, Aelius.

<<HideAll>>
Aelius: (<i>I’m really doing this. I’m going to Mount Olympus to cook for the gods.</i>)
Aelius: (<i>Gods, what am I doing?</i>)
Aelius: (<i>This is either my dumbest idea I’ve ever had, or…</i>)
Aelius: (<i>... Nah, definitely gotta be the dumbest.</i>)
Aelius: (<i>But... whatever. Could be fun, too.)
Aelius: (<i>And I'll get to see my mom again.</i>)
Aelius: (<i>Yeah... this is the right decision.</i>)

// CLOUD BG
// KITCHEN BG
<<Act "Aelius" "Aelius 3_4s" "left" "bottom" #674ea7>>
<<Act "Hestia" "Hestia 3_4s" "right" "bottom" #e06666>>
Hestia: And this is the kitchen. I hope it has everything you should need.
Aelius: This is the biggest kitchen I’ve ever seen…
Aelius: [Positive] Definitely should be more than enough, like <i>damn.</i>
Hestia: I’m glad you like it. Come now, I can show you to your room. I prepared one for you just upstairs.
// AELIUS BEDROOM
Hestia: I do hope you’ll enjoy it here, my dear.
Hestia: You can begin tomorrow. Take the rest of the evening to relax and prepare, at least as much as you can.
Hestia: I’m sure tomorrow will be full of surprises.
Aelius: Thank you, Hestia. I think I’ll be okay.
Hestia: Good. I wish you a good night, Aelius.
Aelius: Night, Hestia.
